    <string name="wl_title">Window/Level in one minute</string>
    <string name="wl_short">Window sets the contrast: how wide the grey range is. Level sets the brightness: where the middle lies.</string>
    <string name="wl_long">A medical image holds far more shades of grey than a screen can show. Window/Level chooses which part you see. A narrow window gives a lot of contrast, a wide window more overview. For CT the app uses fixed presets, such as Lung (L −600, W 1500) and Brain (L 40, W 80). You pick them at the bottom of the viewer.</string>
